==English==
[[Image:Male_whale_shark_at_Georgia_Aquarium.jpg|190px|thumb|right|The large creature in this picture is the '''whale shark''']]
{{wikipedia}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A very large spotted [[shark]], ''[[Rhincodon typus]]'', of warm marine waters, similar to a [[whale]], that feeds by filtering [[plankton]] from the water.
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|title=The Book of Sharks|author={{w|Richard Ellis (biologist)|Richard Ellis}}|year=1983|publisher=Knopf|ISBN=0679722106|passage=The largest fish in the world is a shark. It is a harmless plankton eater, and its name, '''whale shark''' has been confusing people for years.|page=42}}

